[I] Check the syntax of Postgresql SQL files

[T] PgSanity checks the syntax of PostgreSQL SQL files by wrapping them as C
[T] files with embedded SQL and running them through ecpg. This way the
[T] syntax is checked by the exact same parser used by PostgreSQL itself.

[U] https://github.com/markdrago/pgsanity

[A] Pgsanity Authors
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

